    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684-a1">

                <pb facs="0763" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg683"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Signor Prinetti to
                        Mr. Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-05-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 28,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s
                    note of the 25th instant, I have the honor to inform you that the Royal
                    Government has given orders to the competent authorities throughout Italy to
                    accept the good offices of American consuls in behalf of Cuban affairs and Cuban
                    citizens until the Cuban Republic shall send her own representatives to
                    Italy.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prinetti.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
